  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "PASS-01",
      "level": "pass",
      "finding": "V2 has a closed 34-ID expected set; derive and published-entry paths compare the emitted p.175 IDs and approved crop hash set against it. The exact V1 forged prefix mutant is rejected by the registered Books crop tuple guard."
    },
    {
      "id": "PASS-02",
      "level": "pass",
      "finding": "All 12 catalog SHA pins match the current 386b catalogs. Their p.175 regions resolve through the current Books registry with exact source/crop tuple identity; the catalog set has 34 unique p.175 IDs, 8 unique p.175 crop hashes, and 15 total catalog image assets. All 8 p.175 crop assets are byte-hash matched to their catalog and pixel-identical to the pinned private JPEG at the registered bounds, including fd13."
    },
    {
      "id": "PASS-03",
      "level": "pass",
      "finding": "The accepted fd13 left-column crop is registered under the existing Level-of-Characters region ID, p.175/PDF null, source bounds [0,1625,650,1760], and output size 650x135. The old 07fd footer crop tuple is rejected. Crop replacement changes only the available-image set; it does not promote the two legacy context reviews or source/value/mechanics grades."
    },
    {
      "id": "PASS-04",
      "level": "pass",
      "finding": "V2 retains the exact two legacy context IDs, preserves the two-crop monetary screen (deep equality test), leaves p.175 canonical PDF page null, preserves 11 owners/87 table rows (22 p.175, 65 p.176), and carries 120 field targets as pending. The summary now explicitly scopes reviewedCropCount=2 to the legacy context regions."
    },
    {
      "id": "PASS-05",
      "level": "pass",
      "finding": "Copied test-root-v2.mjs passed in an isolated temporary package (6 native tuple negatives, 2 published-evidence negatives, V1 mutant accepted/V2 mutant rejected). The resulting control JSON was byte-identical to the frozen root-control-result-v2.json. No full product build or source-value assessment was run."
    },
    {
      "id": "OPEN-01",
      "level": "integration-guard",
      "finding": "The V2 module and its focused test do not consume/enforce source-catalog-pins-v2.json as an exact per-catalog pin. A cross-owner mutation that swaps the registered left Level-of-Characters region object with the registered Party Size region object between those two catalogs (each catalog count preserved, all tuples/IDs still registered, global closed set unchanged) is accepted at 8 images/34 IDs. The current 12 catalog files match the companion pins, so the observed current output is valid; the code alone does not reject this catalog reassociation unless integration enforces those exact hashes. V3 should bind per-catalog expected region/source tuples or enforce the canonical 12-file pin map."
    },
    {
      "id": "OPEN-02",
      "level": "integration-pending",
      "finding": "This is a projection-module/control package, not an assembled current V28 preview. The current dist/data.json remains the captured 6a data while raw rules.json was updated afterward; source-card coverage still needs fresh reassembly and an actual preview check before release."
    }
  ],
